Spec: Plugin Command Group

Purpose:
  Assemble the `plugin` command group and organize its subcommand modules.

Structure:
  ./plugin.ts: Plugin group assembly.
  ./plugin.test.ts: Plugin group assembly and routing tests.
  ./add.ts: Add subcommand handler.
  ./add.test.ts: Add subcommand argument and help tests.
  ./list.ts: List subcommand handler and output rendering.
  ./list.test.ts: List subcommand options, output, and registry tests.
  ./update.ts: Update subcommand handler.
  ./update.test.ts: Update subcommand argument and help tests.

Owns:
  ./plugin.ts
  ./plugin.test.ts

References:
  ./add.sdd
  ./list.sdd
  ./update.sdd

Must:
  @createPluginCommand receives a @PluginCommandContainer dependency object providing the prebuilt add, list, and update commands.
  @createPluginCommand returns a command named `plugin` and attaches the supplied add, list, and update commands beneath it.
  Group help lists the available subcommands.
  Each subcommand's parsing and service invocation belong in its own same-basename handler and spec in this directory.

Must not:
  @createPluginCommand must not construct subcommand handlers or invoke plugin application services.

Exposes:
  @createPluginCommand
  @PluginCommandContainer
